@startuml
title 3.8.15 Report a handover issue
caption UC-140 | Implemented
skinparam monochrome true
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 0
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam LegendBackgroundColor white
skinparam style strictuml
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
show footbox
<style>
lifeLine {
    LineStyle 0
}
</style>
skinparam sequence {
    ParticipantBackgroundColor white
    ActorBackgroundColor white
    LifeLineBackgroundColor white
    LifeLineBorderColor black
    GroupBackgroundColor white
    GroupHeaderBackgroundColor white
}

' Source: apps/api-node/src/modules/reports/application/report.use-cases.ts
' Main entity migration: apps/api-node/src/migrations/002_lost_found_schema.sql
' One-table abstraction: related repository reads/writes stay inside the service.
actor "Claimant / Finder" as Actor
participant "Appointment Issue Report" as Page
participant "Reports API" as API
participant "Report Service" as Service
participant "reports" as Table <<entity>>

Actor -> Page: 1: Open Report a handover issue
activate Page
Page -> API: 2: POST /api/reports (targetType=HANDOVER)
activate API
API -> API: 3: Validate access session, role and input
alt Valid request
API -> Service: 4: Report a handover issue
activate Service
Service -> Service: 5: Open HANDOVER report from authorized appointment detail
Service -> Service: 6: Validate actual participant, target, category, reason and request\nkey
Service -> Table: 7: INSERT deduplicated HANDOVER report
activate Table
Table --> Service: 8: Pending report
deactivate Table
Service -> Service: 9: Preserve appointment history; block unsafe completion as required
Service --> API: 10: Handover report
API --> Page: 11: HTTP 201: Handover report
Page --> Actor: 12: Show authorized result
deactivate Service
else Invalid input, missing session or insufficient role
API --> Page: 4.1: HTTP 422 / 401 / 403 (429 only if rate-limited)
Page --> Actor: 4.2: Show appropriate error; retain form/draft
end
deactivate API
deactivate Page

legend left
Scope: Dispute/wrong item/unsafe meeting reports use the existing moderation workflow; filing one is
not a completed return.
endlegend
@enduml
